          "number": 1,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "Steel is valued for its reliability, but not when it gets cold. Most forms of steel __(26)__ become brittle(脆的) at temperatures below about -25℃ unless they are mixed with other metals. Now, though, a novel type of steel has been developed that resists __(27)__ at much lower temperatures, while retaining its strength and toughness—without the need for expensive __(28)__ .",
