          "number": 4,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "Perhaps, if we continue to improve information-processing machines, we'll soon have helpful rational assistants. So we must aim to complement the rationality of the machine, rather than to compete with it. If I'm right, we should foster a creative spirit because a dose of illogical creativity will complement the rationality of the machine. Unfortunately, however, our education system has not caught up to the approaching reality. Indeed, our schools and universities are structured to mould pupils to be mostly obedient servants of rationality, and to develop outdated skills in interacting with outdated machines. We need to help our children learn how to best work with smart computers to improve human decision-making. But most of all we need to keep the long-term perspective in mind: that even if computers will outsmart us, we can still be the most creative. Because if we aren't, we won't be providing much value in future ecosystems, and that may put in question the foundation for our existence.",
          "chinese": "或许，如果我们继续改进信息处理机器，很快就会拥有有用的理性助手。因此，我们必须致力于补充机器的理性，而不是与之竞争。如果我的判断是正确的，我们就应当培养创造精神，因为适量的非逻辑性创造力能够补充机器的理性。然而遗憾的是，我们的教育体系还没有跟上这一即将到来的现实。事实上，我们的学校和大学所采用的结构，主要是把学生塑造成理性的顺从仆从，并培养他们使用过时机器进行互动的过时技能。我们需要帮助孩子们学会如何与智能计算机进行最佳协作，从而改善人类的决策。但最重要的是，我们需要牢记长远的视角：即使计算机会在智力上胜过我们，我们仍然可以成为最具创造力的一方。因为如果我们做不到这一点，我们将无法在未来的生态系统中提供太多价值，而这可能会动摇我们存在的基础。",
